Problem Statement
Develop a C++ program to represent mining sites as vertices and candidate pipelines or cables as weighted edges.
Implement Prim’s Algorithm to find the Minimum Spanning Tree (MST) that connects all mining sites with minimum total installation cost.
Modify the program to update an edge weight and apply Prim’s Algorithm again,
display each selected edge with its weight and running total cost, and detect disconnected graphs to determine whether a spanning tree can be formed.
